/* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   QAAPF QUESTION BANK — v4.0 (13 Oct 2026)
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Pure data, no React, so the bank can be checked by a script
   (npm run verify:bank) and imported by the scoring core.

   Fields
     id  stable item ID (domain letter + number). Never reuse an ID;
         retire it and add a new one when an item changes meaning.
     d   domain (A–H)          u  sub-skill unit      t  skill tag
     q   stem                  o  four options        c  index of the key
     lv  difficulty (1 easy, 2 medium, 3 hard), rated by solving effort:
         1 = one step or recall, under 30 s; 2 = two steps or one concept
         applied; 3 = three or more steps, combined ideas or a trap.
     k   "cat" for CAT/XAT-level items: the hardest few, placed last on a paper
     x   worked explanation (all reasoning items and every item added
         from v4.1 on), shown in answer review and the printed key

   Review rule for any change: two people solve the item independently,
   both agree with the key, and the item is self-contained (no "same
   table", no hints in brackets). Keys are spread evenly across A–D.

   v4.3 (15 Oct 2026): hard redefined as placement-advanced (TCS NQT
   Advanced / AMCAT / eLitmus): non-routine, needs an insight or two ideas
   combined. 81 formula-recall items moved hard → medium; 94 new items
   (3 of them later judged medium: B083, D080, D083)
   (62 placement-advanced, 32 CAT/XAT-level, 4 per domain), every answer
   recomputed by code and every puzzle brute-forced to a single solution.

   v4.2 (15 Oct 2026): second-solver review of the 103 v4.1 items — all
   keys correct; C079 and E079 replaced (C083, E082: one needed 18 hours'
   walking, one needed 1.05⁸ by hand); A084, E072, F072 reworded (F072's
   "grandfather" could be either side — old wording voided); 5 items
   re-rated hard → medium; 3 explanations clarified.

   v4.1 changes (15 Oct 2026): every key re-solved — none wrong; 157
   difficulty ratings corrected (most "hard" items were medium); 103 new
   items, mostly hard, including a 41-item reasoning set (coding-decoding,
   blood relations, directions, seating, syllogisms, data sufficiency,
   clocks, calendars, puzzles); explanations on every reasoning item and
   every new item; F016 reworded (two answers were defensible).

   v4 changes: 24 new items (Measurement & Geometry in H, Probability &
   Chance in G); 21 items reworded or repaired. Earlier wordings that
   students may already have answered are listed in QAAPF_LEGACY below
   so their attempts are scored fairly.
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

